  {
   "t": "notice",
   "text": "Draft for Jared’s approval. Figures are closed sales from Jared’s Paragon export; the neighbourhood map outlines are drawn by us and stay draft until each is confirmed.",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Burnaby is split into 35 MLS® sub-areas, the neighbourhood boundaries the Greater Vancouver REALTORS® board uses for every listing and sale. From November 2025 to October 22, 2026, 2,371 homes sold across them: 424 houses, 1,512 condos and 279 townhomes and 156 duplexes. The busiest were Brentwood Park (528), Metrotown (468), Highgate (140).",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "By median price, the houses that sold in Government Road were the most expensive of the 20 Burnaby neighbourhoods with 10 or more house sales ($2,380,000), and those in Highgate the least ($1,500,000). For condos, the range ran from $440,900 in Cariboo to $693,750 in Brentwood Park.",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "These are MLS® sub-areas, not the City of Burnaby’s planning areas, so a neighbourhood here can be larger or smaller than the name suggests. The map and tables below follow the board’s boundaries. Use them to compare areas, then ask Jared for a search set to the exact streets you care about.",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
